- Story & Context: When the trade convoy stalled near the gypsum dunes of Reggane, an overheating generator fried the sequencer of Tariq's patched Roland, threatening to collapse the seasonal synthesizer auction before a single trade was struck. Smelling scorched copper and melted solder under the midday sun, he jammed a desert-dulled pocketknife into the oscillator bypass and instructed Kaveh to blow a repetitive, low French horn drone, birthing a hypnotic, stuttering acid groove that set the entire camp swaying in 104-degree heat. By the time the battery bank cooled down, caravaners had traded three barrels of fuel just to record the session on magnetic tape, shouting along as Mireille leaned into the ribbon mic: "No gear leaves the convoy till the seconds burn down."
